\"再次開始\". Keep board rendered as-is.\n\nPause toggle: if playing → paused + overlay \"已暫停\" + button resume; if paused → playing + hide overlay.\n\nRestart button also in HUD (\"重新開始\") and \"暫停\" button.\n\nKeyboard: In paused state, 'p' resumes, Enter/Space starts? Enter starts (fresh start) or resume? Let's: in menu, Space/Enter starts. In paused, Space/Enter resumes. In over, Space/Enter/R restarts.\n\nKeydown handler logic:\n\n```js\nif (gameState === 'menu') { if (k==='Enter'||k===' ') { e.preventDefault(); startGame(); } return; }\nif (gameState === 'over') { if (k==='Enter'||k===' '||k==='r'||k==='R') { startGame(); } return; }\nif (gameState === 'paused') { if (k==='Enter'||k===' '||k==='p'||k==='P') togglePause(); return; }\n// playing\n```\n\nBut preventDefault for arrows/space regardless — handle before state checks.\n\nAlso 'KeyP' — use e.key with letters; Chinese input? Keep e.key.\n\nNote: preventDefault on space/arrows before other logic.\n\nSoft drop bonus: while soft, score += 1 per grounded move. Implement in step():\n\n```js\nfunction step() {\n  if (!collides(current.matrix, current.x, current.y + 1)) {\n    current.y++;\n    if (softActive()) score++;\n  } else {\n    lockPiece();\n  }\n}\n```\n\nNote soft Active should be evaluated at step time via current held state, not tick-time. Fine.\n\nlockPiece:\n\n```js\nfunction lockPiece() {\n  const m = current.matrix;\n  for (let y = 0; y < m.length; y++) for (let x = 0; x < m[y].length; x++) {\n    if (m[y][x]) {\n      const gy = current.y + y, gx = current.x + x;\n      if (gy >= 0 && gy < ROWS && gx >= 0 && gx < COLS) grid[gy][gx] = current.color;\n    }\n  }\n  clearLines();\n  current = next;\n  next = drawNext();\n  dropAccum = 0;\n  dropInterval = Math.max(80, 900 - (level - 1) * 70);\n  if (collides(current.matrix, current.x, current.y)) gameOver();\n  updateHUD();\n}\n```\n\nclearLines:\n\n```js\nfunction clearLines() {\n  let count = 0;\n  for (let y = ROWS - 1; y >= 0; y--) {\n    if (grid[y].every(cell => cell !== null)) {\n      grid.splice(y, 1);\n      grid.unshift(Array(COLS).fill(null));\n      count++;\n      y++; // re-check same index? Since splice shifts, after splice this y now contains the row that was below... unshift adds empty at top shifting everything down. Simpler: re-check y. After splice+unshift, grid length same; row y now is the row that was y+1? Let's see: before: rows ..., y:[full], y+1:[x]. Remove y: rows ..., y:[x] (former y+1). unshift: rows:[empty], ..., y-1:[old y-1], y:[empty?] hmm... \n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nHmm after splice+unshift, the row we just cleared is gone; the loop then checks next y from bottom. Let me instead iterate y from bottom, and if full, remove and unshift, then continue with y unchanged but decrement after? Let me just do a simpler merge-style approach:\n\n```js\nconst newGrid = [];\nfor (let y = 0; y < ROWS; y++) {\n  if (grid[y].every(c => c)) { lines++; }\n  else newGrid.unshift(grid[y]);\n}\nconst cleared = lines - prevLines... \n```\n\nCleaner:\n\n```js\nfunction clearLines() {\n  let cleared = 0;\n  for (let y = ROWS - 1; y >= 0; y--) {\n    if (grid[y].every(c => c)) {\n      grid.splice(y, 1);\n      grid.unshift(Array(COLS).fill(null));\n      cleared++;\n    }\n  }\n  ...\n}\n```\n\nProblem: after splicing row y and unshifting, the rows shift; iterating down with y-- would recheck the row now at y which is old y+1... wait after splice(y,1) the row at index y becomes old row y+1 (since rows below shifted up). Then unshift puts a new empty row at index 0, so all rows shift down by 1: empty at 0, ..., old row y+1 at y+1. Iterating y-- from bottom: we'd skip checking rows above y (they were shifted? no—unshift pushes everything down including rows above y). Hmm rows above y are now one index lower... Let me think: before operation: [0..ROW-1]. Row y full. splice removes row y → array now has ROWS-1 rows: indexes 0..y-1 (same), 0..: index y now holds old y+1, ..., index ROWS-2 holds old ROWS-1. Then unshift(empty) → ROWS rows: index 0 empty, index 1..y same as old 0..y-1, index y+1..ROWS-1 = old y..ROWS-2? Wait: unshift adds at index 0, shifting all other rows +1. So index 1..y+1 = original 0..y (post-splice array: indexes 0..y-1, then old y+1 at y, ...). Post-splice indexes: 0..y-1 (same as before), y = old y+1, y+1 = old y+2, ..., ROWS-2 = old ROWS-1. After unshift: index 1 = old index 0, ..., index j+1 = old index j. So index y-1 = old y-2, index y = old y-1, index y+1 = old y+1(=old y+1 shifted). The full row at y is removed; other full rows still present but shifted down. Iterating y from ROWS-1 downward with y-- : we'd check ROW-1 (empty), ROW-2... Actually after the operation, we'd continue y-- from where? We're in the iteration; if we set y++ we'd recheck... Iterating downward means y decreases; after handling row y, next y-1... wait we iterate from bottom up? Let me do top-down and avoid loop mutation issues by reconstructing:\n\n```js\nfunction clearLines() {\n  let cleared = 0;\n  const rows = [];\n  for (let y = 0; y < ROWS; y++) {\n    if (grid[y].every(c => c)) cleared++;\n    else rows.push(grid[y]);\n  }\n  while (rows.length < ROWS) rows.unshift(Array(COLS).fill(null));\n  grid = rows;\n  if (cleared > 0) {\n    lines += cleared;\n    score += [0, 100, 300, 500, 800][cleared] * level;\n    const newLevel = Math.floor(lines / 10) + 1;\n    if (newLevel > level) level = newLevel;\n    dropInterval = Math.max(80, 900 - (level - 1) * 70);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThis is clean. \n\nAlso on hard drop, lines scoring uses same.\n\nupdateHUD: score, lines, level, and next preview (render next each frame or on change). Canvas rendering every frame is fine.\n\nRender loop:\n\n```js\nfunction loop(ts) {\n  if (!lastTime) lastTime = ts;\n  const dt = ts - lastTime;\n  lastTime = ts;\n  if (gameState === 'playing') {\n    const soft = softKey || softTouch;\n    const interval = soft ? SOFT_MS : dropInterval;\n    dropAccum += dt;\n    while (dropAccum >= interval) {\n      dropAccum -= interval;\n      step(soft);\n      if (gameState !== 'playing') break; // game over during step\n    }\n  }\n  render();\n  requestAnimationFrame(loop);\n}\n```\n\nsoft passed to step so scoring only when soft held at step time. OK.\n\nEdge: step() can call lockPiece → current = next etc. If game over, state changes mid-loop; break.\n\nRender: draws board + next preview. Called each frame regardless — fine.\n\nPause: set gameState='paused', show overlay. Resume hides overlay.\n\nRender also shows pause overlay via DOM (not canvas). Good.\n\nNow overlays: \n\n```html\n<div id=\"overlay\" class=\"overlay\">\n  <div class=\"overlay-card\">\n    <h2 id=\"overlay-title\"></h2>\n    <p id=\"overlay-text\"></p>\n    <button id=\"overlay-btn\"></button>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\nCSS: overlay covers board area only (absolutely positioned in board-wrap). Actually cover whole game-wrap? Cover board canvas region is neat.\n\nButton click handler: depends on state: menu → start; paused → resume; over → restart.\n\nHUD buttons: 暫停/繼續 toggles; 重新開始 starts fresh.\n\nTouch controls markup:\n\n```html\n<div class=\"touch-controls\">\n  <button data-act=\"left\">◀</button>\n  <button data-act=\"down\" id=\"btn-soft\">▼</button>\n  <button data-act=\"rotate\">🔄</button> // maybe '↻'\n  <button data-act=\"right\">▶</button>\n  <button data-act=\"hard\">⏬</button> // 硬降\n</div>\n```\n\nUse text glyphs: ◀ ▶ ↻ ▼ ⇹? Let me use: 左 右 rotate ▼ 強制下. Use simple characters: ◀ ▶ ↻ ▼ ⚡? Keep: `◀`, `▶`, `↻`, `▼`, `⇊`? Font support... use ASCII-ish: \"‹\" \"›\"? I'll use: 左 右 旋轉 下 硬降 with icons: ◀ ▶ ↻ ▼ ⤓. Let me just use text: \"←\" \"→\" \"↻\" \"▼\" \"⤓\"? The arrows ←→ are common. Buttons: `←` `→` `↻` `▼`(下) `⤓`(硬降). Fine.\n\nTouch events: attach 'pointerdown' and 'pointerup'/'pointerleave'/'pointercancel'. For rotate/hard/left/right: click. For down: pointerdown → softTouch = true, pointerup → false.\n\nNote: click fires after touch; fine. Use e.preventDefault() on pointerdown to avoid double events and scrolling. For left/right/rotate/hard, pointerdown handler directly better (immediate response, no 300ms delay). So: left/right/rotate/hard: pointerdown → action. down: pointerdown/up/leave → softTouch. Also for down, also handle pointercancel.\n\nAlso prevent context menu on long press: `touch-action: none` and preventDefault.\n\nNow the start menu overlay text: \"俄羅斯方塊\" + \"按 Enter 或點擊開始\" + button \"開始遊戲\".\n\nNow, board rendering details:\n\n```js\nfunction render() {\n  bctx.clearRect? fill background\n  bctx.fillStyle = '#0d1322'; fillRect.\n  // grid lines\n  bctx.strokeStyle = 'rgba(148,163,184,0.07)';\n  for i in 0..COLS: vertical line; for j in 0..ROWS: horizontal.\n  // locked cells\n  for r,c: if grid[r][c] drawCell(...)\n  // ghost\n  if (gameState === 'playing' || 'paused') and current: compute ghostY; draw ghost with alpha 0.25\n  // current piece\n  if current: for cells drawCell(current.color)\n}\n```\n\nDuring paused, still draw current. During 'over', keep board drawn. During menu, draw empty grid.\n\nGhost only when playing/paused and current exists.\n\nAlso add lines progress? Keep simple.\n\nHUD: 分數, 等級, 行數， 下一個 preview.\n\nFont: font-family: 'Segoe UI', 'Noto Sans TC', sans-serif.\n\nCanvas sizing: board 300x600 CSS, maybe scaled up on small screens.\n\nAdd subtle CRT/glow? Keep classy.\n\nShake on 4-line clear? Nice extra: flash lines. Could add simple effect: store clearedRowsTimestamp to flash. Keep simple: skip.\n\nLet me also handle window blur → pause? Auto-pause on blur is good. Add window.addEventListener('blur', () => { if playing → pause }).\n\nNow write the whole file. Must be complete — avoid truncation. Let me aim for a reasonably compact but complete file (~450-550 lines). Ensure no external resources.\n\nWrite CSS:\n\n```css\n:root {\n  --bg:#070b14; --panel:#111a2c; --border:#26334f; --text:#e6edf7; --muted:#8b9bb4; --accent:#22d3ee; --accent2:#a78bfa;\n}\n*{box-sizing:border-box}\nhtml,body{height:100%}\nbody{\n  margin:0; font-family:'Segoe UI','Noto Sans TC',sans-serif;\n  background: radial-gradient(1200px 800px at 50% -10%, #16233f 0%, var(--bg) 60%);\n  color: var(--text);\n  min-height:100vh; display:flex; flex-direction:column; align-items:center; justify-content:center;\n  padding:20px 12px; gap:14px;\n}\nh1{ font-size: 28px; letter-spacing: 4px; margin: 0; text-align:center; font-weight:800; text-shadow: 0 0 18px rgba(34,211,238,.45);}\nh1 span{ color:var(--accent); }\n.game-wrap{ display:flex; gap:14px; align-items:flex-start; }\n.panel{ background: linear-gradient(180deg,#152036, #101829); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:14px; padding:14px; width:150px; box-shadow: 0 10px 30px rgba(0,0,0,.45); }\n.stat{ margin-bottom:14px; }\n.stat .label{ font-size:11px; color:var(--muted); letter-spacing:2px; text-transform:uppercase; margin-bottom:2px;}\n.stat .value{ font-size:22px; font-weight:700; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }\n.board-wrap{ position:relative; }\ncanvas#board{ display:block; border-radius:12px; border:1px solid #2b3a57; box-shadow: 0 14px 40px rgba(0,0,0,.55), inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.03); background:#0b1120;}\n#next{display:block;margin:0 auto; border:1px dashed #2b3a57; border-radius:8px; background:#0b1120;}\n.panel button{ width:100%; padding:8px; margin-top:8px; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid var(--border); background:#1b2740; color:var(--text); cursor:pointer; font-size:13px;}\n.panel button:hover{ background:#233453;}\n.overlay{ position:absolute; inset:0; display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; background:rgba(6,10,20,.78); backdrop-filter: blur(3px); border-radius:12px; z-index:5;}\n.overlay.hidden{ display:none; }\n.overlay-card{ text-align:center; padding:20px; max-width: 240px;}\n.overlay-card h2{ font-size:26px; margin:0 0 10px; letter-spacing:2px; color:#fff;}\n.overlay-card p{ color:var(--muted); font-size:14px; line-height:1.6; margin:0 0 18px;}\n.overlay-card button{ padding:10px 26px; border-radius:10px; border:none; background: linear-gradient(180deg,#2dd4ee,#0ea5b7); color:#052831; font-weight:700; font-size:16px; cursor:pointer; box-shadow:0 6px 18px rgba(34,211,238,.35);}\n.overlay-card button:hover{ filter:brightness(1.1); }\n.touch-controls{ display:flex; gap:8px; flex-wrap:wrap; justify-content:center; max-width: 320px; }\n.touch-controls button{ width:56px; height:48px; border-radius:10px; border:1px solid var(--border); background:#1b2740; color:var(--text); font-size:18px; touch-action:none; user-select:none; -webkit-user-select:none; cursor:pointer; }\n.touch-controls button:active{ background:#2a3b5e; }\nkbd-hints: small text under: \"操作：←/→ 移動 · ↑ 旋轉 · ↓ 軟降 · 空白 硬降 · P 暫停\"\n.hint{ font-size:12px; color:var(--muted); text-align:center; letter-spacing:1px;}\n@media (max-width: 700px){ .game-wrap{ flex-direction: column; align-items:center;} .panel{ width: min(300px, 86vw); display:flex; gap:10px; ...} }\n```\n\nHmm on mobile, side panels stack above/below. Simpler: keep flex-wrap. Let me make game-wrap wrap and panels have min width. I'll make a reasonable responsive rule: flex-direction column, panels full width with stats inline.\n\nFine, keep moderately simple responsive.\n\nTouch controls: show only on touch devices? Use media (pointer: coarse). Also allow always show? Show only on coarse pointers to keep desktop clean:\n\n```css\n.touch-controls{ display:none; }\n@media (pointer: coarse){ .touch-controls{ display:flex; } }\n```\n\nGood.\n\nNow full JS. Let me write carefully, mentally checking.\n\n```js\nconst COLS = 10, ROWS = 20, CELL = 30;\nconst SOFT_MS = 40;\n\nconst SHAPES = [\n  { name:'I', color:'#22d3ee', matrix: [ [1,1,1,1] ] },\n  { name:'O', color:'#facc15', matrix: [ [1,1],[1,1] ] },\n  { name:'T', color:'#c084fc', matrix: [ [0,1,0],[1,1,1] ] },\n  { name:'S', color:'#4ade80', matrix: [ [0,1,1],[1,1,0] ] },\n  { name:'Z', color:'#f87171', matrix: [ [1,1,0],[0,1,1] ] },\n  { name:'J', color:'#60a5fa', matrix: [ [1,0,0],[1,1,1] ] },\n  { name:'L', color:'#fb923c', matrix: [ [0,0,1],[1,1,1] ] },\n];\n\nconst board = document.getElementById('board');\nconst bctx = board.getContext('2d');\nconst nextCanvas = document.getElementById('nextCanvas');\nconst nctx = nextCanvas.getContext('2d');\nconst elScore = document.getElementById('score');\nconst elLines = document.getElementById('lines');\nconst elLevel = document.getElementById('level');\nconst overlay = document.getElementById('overlay');\nconst overlayTitle = document.getElementById('overlay-title');\nconst overlayText = document.getElementById('overlay-text');\nconst overlayBtn = document.getElementById('overlay-btn');\n\nlet grid, bag, current, next, score, lines, level, dropInterval, dropAccum, gameState, lastTs;\nlet softKey = false, softTouch = false;\n```\n\nnextCanvas dims: width=120 height=80. Cell 24.\n\nFunctions:\n\n```js\nfunction makeMatrix(m){ return m.map(r => r.slice()); }\nfunction refillBag(){\n  const indices = [0,1,2,3,4,5,6];\n  for (let i = indices.length - 1; i > 0; i--) {\n    const j = Math.floor(Math.random() * (i + 1));\n    [indices[i], indices[j]] = [indices[j], indices[i]];\n  }\n  bag = indices.map(i => SHAPES[i]);\n}\nfunction drawFromBag(){\n  if (!bag || bag.length === 0) refillBag();\n  const shape = bag.pop();\n  const matrix = makeMatrix(shape.matrix);\n  return {\n    name: shape.name,\n    color: shape.color,\n    matrix,\n    x: Math.floor((COLS - matrix[0].length) / 2),\n    y: 0\n  };\n}\n```\n\nHmm, for I spawn at row 0 with the single-row matrix — could collide with stack at row 0 → gameover. Correct.\n\nActually maybe spawn y for piece so its bottom is at top. It's fine.\n\nrotate helpers:\n\n```js\nfunction rotateCW(m){\n  const R = m.length, C = m[0].length;\n  const out = Array.from({length: C}, () => Array(R).fill(0));\n  for (let y = 0; y < R; y++) for (let x = 0; x < C; x++) out[x][R - 1 - y] = m[y][x];\n  return out;\n}\nfunction rotateCCW(m){\n  const R = m.length, C = m[0].length;\n  const out = Array.from({length: C}, () => Array(R).fill(0));\n  for (let y = 0; y < R; y++) for (let x = 0; x < C; x++) out[C - 1 - x][y] = m[y][x];\n  return out;\n}\n```\n\ncollides:\n\n```js\nfunction collides(matrix, px, py){\n  for (let y = 0; y < matrix.length; y++){\n    for (let x = 0; x < matrix[y].length; x++){\n      if (!matrix[y][x]) continue;\n      const gx = px + x, gy = py + y;\n      if (gx < 0 || gx >= COLS || gy >= ROWS) return true;\n      if (gy >= 0 && grid[gy][gx]) return true;\n    }\n  }\n  return false;\n}\n```\n\ntryRotate:\n\n```js\nfunction tryRotate(dir){\n  if (!current) return;\n  const rotated = dir === 1 ? rotateCW(current.matrix) : rotateCCW(current.matrix);\n  const kicks = [{dx:0,dy:0},{dx:-1,dy:0},{dx:1,dy:0},{dx:0,dy:1},{dx:-2,dy:0},{dx:2,dy:0},{dx:-1,dy:1},{dx:1,dy:1}];\n  for (const k of kicks){\n    if (!collides(rotated, current.x + k.dx, current.y + k.dy)){\n      current.matrix = rotated;\n      current.x += k.dx;\n      current.y += k.dy;\n      return;\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nmove:\n\n```js\nfunction move(dx){ if (current && !collides(current.matrix, current.x + dx, current.y)) current.x += dx; }\n```\n\nghostY:\n\n```js\nfunction ghostY(){\n  if (!current) return 0;\n  let y = current.y;\n  while (!collides(current.matrix, current.x, y + 1)) y++;\n  return y;\n}\n```\n\nhardDrop:\n\n```js\nfunction hardDrop(){\n  if (gameState !== 'playing' || !current) return;\n  const g = ghostY();\n  score += (g - current.y) * 2;\n  current.y = g;\n  lockPiece();\n}\n```\n\nstep:\n\n```js\nfunction step(soft){\n  if (!current) return;\n  if (!collides(current.matrix, current.x, current.y + 1)){\n    current.y++;\n    if (soft) score++;\n  } else lockPiece();\n}\n```\n\nlockPiece:\n\n```js\nfunction lockPiece(){\n  const m = current.matrix;\n  for (let y = 0; y < m.length; y++) for (let x = 0; x < m[y].length; x++){\n    if (!m[y][x]) continue;\n    const gy = current.y + y, gx = current.x + x;\n    if (